meta {
  name: Get ADX Values
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/adx/aapl?timespan=D
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timespan: D
  ~period: 14
  ~threshold: 25
  ~rising: 3
  ~sessions: RTH
  ~bars: 50
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Get ADX / +DI / −DI Values
  
  Computes Wilder's Directional Movement system per bar so you can verify the
  values against a charting platform and see where trends turn. This endpoint
  does NOT place orders — it is for inspection/validation only.
  
  - **+DI / −DI** give DIRECTION (whichever is on top is the dominant side).
  - **ADX** gives STRENGTH (higher = stronger trend; direction-agnostic).
  - **diCross** flags a DI crossover: `UP` = +DI crossed above −DI (bullish
    up-turn), `DOWN` = −DI crossed above +DI (bearish down-turn).
  - **pattern** flags one of two setups (see below).
  
  Any US stock symbol works (the ticker need NOT be in the watchlist).
  
  ## Query
  All indicator params default from config (`webull.adx.*`); pass them only to
  override per request.
  - `period`    — DI/ADX lookback (default from `webull.adx.period`, 14).
  - `threshold` — ADX level separating weak/ranging from trending (default from
    `webull.adx.threshold`, 25).
  - `rising`    — bars back ADX is compared against to judge "rising" (default
    from `webull.adx.rising`, 3).
  - `timespan`  — bar granularity (default M1). Supported: M1, M5, M15, M30,
    M60, M120, M240, D, W, M, Y.
  - `sessions`  — trading sessions (comma-separated). Supported: RTH, PRE,
    ATH, OVN. Omit to use the configured default.
  - `count`     — number of bars to fetch (default = webull.trading.warmup-bars).
  - `bars`      — how many most-recent points to return (default 50; use 0 for all).
  
  ## Patterns flagged
  - `LOW_ADX_RISING`   — ADX below `threshold` but rising over the last `rising`
    bars: a trend may be waking up before it is confirmed. Trade the anticipation.
  - `HIGH_ADX_REVERSAL` — a DI crossover while ADX is at/above `threshold`
    (strong existing trend): a meaningful reversal rather than noise.
  
  ## Response (200)
  { ticker, period, threshold, risingLookback, timespan, sessions, barsFetched,
    latestPlusDi, latestMinusDi, latestAdx, latestDirection, latestDiCross,
    latestPattern, latestClose, returned,
    series: [ { timestamp, timestampEt, close, plusDi, minusDi, adx,
                diCross (UP|DOWN|null), direction (UP|DOWN|FLAT),
                pattern (LOW_ADX_RISING|HIGH_ADX_REVERSAL|null) } ] }
  
  Warm-up bars carry null plusDi/minusDi (first DI ~ index `period`) and null
  adx (first ADX ~ index 2*period-1).
  
  ## Errors
  - `400` — invalid period/threshold/rising/timespan/session, or not enough bars
    (needs at least 2*period).
  - `502` — Webull market-data error.
  - `503` — no bars returned.
}
